    25 and 27; the text layer agreed on each.
  - Shape: chiang-ku-dragon''s, which the sibling batch (kukulcan-dragon, lo-dox-dragon,
    night-stalker-dragon) also follows - a hatchling and an adult variant, each carrying
    attribute dice, pools, horror factor and bonuses (attacks_base included). The top-level
    skills, magic and psionics are the hatchling''s, because printed 50 makes only the
    hatchling a player character and a variant cannot override magic or psionics; the
    adult''s psionics and magic are special abilities. The adult variant''s skill_overrides
    restate the percentages the adult prints. starting_money 0 and equipment_starting []
    are printed 50''s "start with no possessions".
  - xp_table: the Dragon Exp. Table, printed 17, read off a render; lower bounds 0 / 3,001 /
    5,001 / 10,001 / 20,001 / 30,001 / 50,001 / 80,001 / 120,001 / 170,001 / 230,001 /
    300,001 / 380,001 / 470,001 / 600,001 - the same ladder RUE''s dragon-hatchling stores.
    The table runs to level 30; the app stores 15.
  - Attributes (hatchling) as printed. Spd 5D6; no hatchling flying speed is printed (the
    adult flies at 2D6x10+80).
  - Hit points 1D4x100, S.D.C. 5D6x10 plus 3D6 per level, P.P.E. 2D4x10 plus 10 per level,
    Horror Factor 12. sdc_base is stated, so no men_of_arms line.
  - Bonuses are in addition to attribute bonuses. "+1 on all other saving throws" is written
    out across the fourteen d20 saves, as on the Gargoyle Lord; coma_death_pct is a
    percentage and is left out.
  - Attacks: four physical, stored as attacks_base 4. No hand to hand skill is granted, the
    related picks exclude hand to hand combat skills (except_prefix "Hand to Hand:"), and
    no style is sold (costs {}).
  - Skills: the adult''s R.C.C. skills with the hatchling rule on the same page - language
    and basic math at 96%, domestic skills, advanced math and everything else at first level
    proficiency, which is catalog base plus the printed bonus. "Literate in Dragonese/Elven
    and four other languages ... plus speaks six additional languages": Dragonese is granted
    spoken and written; the four literacies are Literacy: Other; the spoken languages are
    ten Language: Other picks, the four it reads plus the six additional (judgement - the
    catalog does not pair a literacy with its spoken language). Scholar/Technical is the
    Technical category. The 14 selections are occ_related_skills, the shape RUE''s
    dragon-hatchling uses.
  - Psionics: minor, six powers "from either the sensitive or physical category", read as a
    pick from both; two more at fifth level and two at tenth. I.S.P. 1D6x10 plus M.E.
  - Magic: the hatchling knows no spells (spells_starting 0, the shape of the RUE hatchlings
    that say the same). "By 2nd level ... 3D4+3 spells from levels 1-3" describes learning,
    not a grant, and is prose in Magic Knowledge. The adult and NPC-hatchling spell lists
    and the second-discipline table are a special ability.
  - The language and literacy picks carry the printed percentage as a bonus over the
    catalog''s Other rows (Language: Other 50%, Literacy: Other 30%), so each pick starts at
    the printed figure and still climbs; regression refuses a language pick frozen by base.
  - The adult: attacks_base on the adult variant from its printed attacks per melee - eight physical, or four fire breath and four physical, or two by magic.
    Its "+N on all other saving throws" is written out the same way.
  - Natural A.R. is prose (no key); horror_factor is stated on each variant.
---

## Lore

The Fire Dragon is a massive reptilian creature of vaguely humanoid shape, with powerful limbs, great bat-like wings, a long tail and a row of fins down its spine from the back of the head to mid-tail. Its fine scales run from crimson to alizarin red. Fire dragons are among the keenest students of magic of all dragons, and among the most likely to use human technology, jewelry and "machines of men" - though no gadget is ever worthy of the primary treasure hoard.

A hatchling is powerful by human standards but only a fraction of the adult it will become: naive, brash, emotional and curious, roughly the equivalent of a young child in understanding of the world.

**Alignment:** Any, but tends toward selfish.

**Size (adult):** 20 to 30 feet (6 to 9 m) tall, up to 65 feet (20 m) long, wingspan 100 feet (30.5 m).

**Weight (adult):** 25 tons.

**Habitat:** Anywhere, but prefers warm climates; rarely met in the Great Northern Wilderness, the Land of the Damned, Phi, Lopan or the northern half of the Eastern Territory.

**Average Life Span:** 6000 years; some have reached 9000.

**Enemies:** None per se.

**Allies:** Amazingly tolerant of other dragons (other than Fire Dragons), with an affinity for the giant races, including Ogres and Trolls.

## GM Notes

Average experience level of an adult is 2D4+5. The adult variant carries the adult''s attributes (Spd 2D6x10 running, 2D6x10+80 flying), pools, horror factor and bonuses; its psionics and magic are special abilities.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'fire-dragon');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'fire-dragon';

